# A template of a script: `mise run ffi-test` copies `note.txt` into a
# temporary directory with a `.project` marker beside it, so the marker
# adapter finds a workspace there without git, writes this file there with
# `@FILE@` replaced by the copy's absolute path, and runs it against
# `stores-config/` with `--state` naming a fresh directory beside it. It
# bumps a store kept across a restart and one that is not, runs `:!true` in
# the file's workspace, starts the job `hold`, which a person waits on and
# which is still running, types, waits until the session index and the
# journal are written (`indexed`, `journalled`) and aborts: the process
# ends with the status 134 and no shutdown. `stores-restore-script`, run
# next with the same `--state`, restores them. What it prints must be
# exactly `stores-expected`, the temporary directory read as `@DIR@`.

reload
settle

# `:e` opens the file; its load and its workspace's finder are jobs, and
# each change they make starts a write of the index: `indexed` waits for
# them all.
key : Semicolon shift
commit e @FILE@
key <Enter> Enter -
indexed

# `kept` is bumped twice and `unkept` once.
run bump-kept
run bump-kept
run bump-unkept

# `:!true` runs in the file's workspace and is remembered in its project's
# history (`shell-history`).
key : Semicolon shift
commit !true
key <Enter> Enter -
indexed

# `hold` sleeps a minute on the job clock: it is running when the process
# ends.
spawn hold

# Typed in insert state, so the file's text is unsaved.
key i KeyI -
key x KeyX -
key <Escape> Escape -
indexed
journalled
abort
